@@ -101,6 +101,23 @@ Set `BASE_URL` to the full URL where your Fizzy instance is accessible:
 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can send everything that lands in someone's notification tray to their phone and desktop as a push notification.
+Browsers only accept pushes that are signed with a VAPID key pair, so you need to generate one for your instance and keep using the same pair:
+
+```sh
+docker run --rm fizzy bin/rails push:keys
+```
+
+Set the two values it prints as environment variables:
+
+- `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY`
+- `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY`
+
+Until they're set, the "This Device" section of notification settings stays hidden and no pushes are sent.
+People turn notifications on per device from that section.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
